WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.200
Alright guys, so in this video we are going to talk about breaker blocks. It is another entry pattern that you can use

00:10.560 --> 00:14.520
It is very powerful. So what essentially is breaker block?

00:16.200 --> 00:18.540
When you have a lower low

00:19.720 --> 00:23.320
lower high lower low and a market structure shift

00:24.960 --> 00:26.960
So when you had lower low

00:27.680 --> 00:29.320
lower high

00:29.320 --> 00:31.880
lower low, the last lower low

00:35.640 --> 00:40.400
And the last candle of that lower low right here

00:43.920 --> 00:48.800
Is your breaker block. So you have lower low lower high lower low and

00:50.160 --> 00:57.040
Market structure shift if you have another small lower low here like lower low lower high small lower high lower low

00:57.120 --> 01:01.320
And then market structure shift then that would be your breaker block. So

01:03.000 --> 01:05.360
The first candle right here

01:08.000 --> 01:12.360
First candle before this move or you could say the last candle

01:13.240 --> 01:16.240
before this last lower low is

01:17.560 --> 01:21.600
Your breaker block and if there is some

01:21.840 --> 01:25.880
Fairbody gap here, then that breaker block becomes very strong

01:26.320 --> 01:32.520
However, if there is no fairbody gap, you can still take entry from this level, okay?

01:33.320 --> 01:38.360
But if there's fairbody gap then that becomes even better price comes back here and boom

01:39.560 --> 01:45.040
Similarly, you have higher high high low higher high market structure shift

01:45.960 --> 01:47.960
this

01:48.080 --> 01:50.080
last candle

01:50.880 --> 01:55.800
Before the move to the upside and then market structure shift. So you have higher high high low

01:56.680 --> 02:01.720
The last candle of the higher low is your breaker block, okay?

02:02.360 --> 02:05.840
Price comes back here if there is fairbody gap right here

02:05.840 --> 02:11.480
You can literally take your entry from here instead of looking for entry from the extreme fairbody gap

02:11.680 --> 02:15.720
What you can do as an entry model you can look for entry here

02:15.760 --> 02:20.320
so a lot of people asking me we miss sometimes we miss the trade and

02:21.080 --> 02:23.080
this is how you can

02:23.680 --> 02:26.840
minimize the risk of missing the trade

02:27.360 --> 02:32.040
Yes, your stop loss going to be big or you can just put your stop above the breaker block

02:32.040 --> 02:36.880
But trust me you're gonna lose so just put it above the fair extreme fairbody gap

